elpa-welkomscherm (1.5.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pass the test suite in an Emacs that can display no glyph: the icon tests
    pin `char-displayable-p' instead of asking a batch Emacs with no fonts,
    which made `icons-draw-before-*' fail in a sandbox.
  * Bump the version to 1.5.3.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:20:00 +0100

elpa-welkomscherm (1.5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Turn the banner off by default: `welkomscherm/show-banner' now defaults
    to nil, so no frame draws a banner above the greeting until it is
    enabled.
  * Bump the version to 1.5.2.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:55:00 +0100

elpa-welkomscherm (1.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Try the PNG splash logo Emacs installs when the build cannot draw the
    SVG one, before dropping the banner image at all.
  * Make the ASCII banner opt-in: `welkomscherm/banner-ascii' now defaults
    to nil, so terminals, batch renders and the screenshots show no banner.
  * Bump the version to 1.5.1.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0100

elpa-welkomscherm (1.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a banner at the top of the screen: the GNU Emacs splash logo in a
    frame that can display images, `welkomscherm/banner-ascii' elsewhere.
    It is on by default; disable it with `welkomscherm/show-banner'.
  * Add opt-in plain-text icons for bookmarks, work links and actions:
    `welkomscherm/icons', `welkomscherm/icon-list' and
    `welkomscherm/icon-fallback'.
  * The default section list now begins with `welkomscherm/banner-section'.
  * Bump the version to 1.5.0.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100

